SUMMARY:You Asked ....... We Got 'Em!!!
DESCRIPTION:That’s right folks\, you too could own one of these stylish hats and at the same time\, become an ambassador for the Asheville area’s favorite local music calendar! \nThese distressed trucker hats are modeled after the way we live. Designed with a relaxed casual fit to move with our busy\, or not so busy\, lifestyle. \nAfter three years of wearing nearly everyday\, mine still holds it’s form. Simply place it on the top rack of your dishwasher every now and then to keep it clean. \nAvailable in our traditional grey or now in faded navy. \nJust $20 including tax plus $5 shipping or free local drop-off (yup\, we live here and will be happy to meet you). \nPlace your order with us at livemusicasheville@gmail.com \nThanks For Your Support!!! \nVenmo: click here  \nLast 4 digits – 3383 \nPayPal: click here \n \n  \n  \n 
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/you-asked-we-got-em/2026-07-12/
LOCATION:LiveMusicAsheville.com\, ASHEVILLE\, NC\, 28803\, United States
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/IMG_8875-scaled-e1778342260940.jpeg
GEO:35.5671423;-82.5437614
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:LiveMusicAsheville.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260714
DTSTAMP:20260705T223640Z
CREATED:20260703T152750Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260705T223640Z
UID:10072902-1783825200-1783911599@livemusicasheville.com
SUMMARY:COMING JULY 18th & 19th | All Jammed Up Music Festival
DESCRIPTION:July 18th &19th\, 2026 | One World Brewing West | Tickets from $30.00 click here! \nThe All Jammed Up Fest is back BIGGER and BETTER this year with Kendall Street Company headlining Saturday and Sicard Hollow headlining Sunday. Plus\, touring bands like Frute and Keep\, as well as staples of the Asheville music scene – Suns of Stars\, Strictly Liquid\, and more!\n\nPresented by All Jammed Up\, this special two-night party celebrates community and the joy of live music. Come kick your shoes off\, dance your heart out\, and support local artists and vendors! You’re not gonna want to miss it!\n\n\n\nVirginia’s Kendall Street Company are no strangers to having a wild time. The genre-fluid\, eclectic rock ensemble has drawn varied comparisons to the dynamic jams of Umphrey’s McGee and Widespread Panic\, songwriting prowess of John Prine\, experimental psychedelia of Pink Floyd\, progressive jazz-infused rock of Frank Zappa\, and off-color humor of Ween and They Might Be Giants. Including elements of crowd participation\, off-the-cuff comedic bits\, haphazard choreography\, musical improvisation\, and surprise musical guests\, each Kendall Street Company concert is an experience unlike any other. You’ll laugh\, you’ll cry. Just remember to stay hydrated.\n\nNashville’s psychedelic punk-grass rockers\, Sicard Hollow\, is a four-piece progressive bluegrass band who formed with a mutual passion for pushing the boundaries of genre. Heavily influenced by the Grateful Dead and New Grass Revival\, these young pickers bring new energy to a timeless style with a combination of fearless improvisation and instrumental prowess.\n\nFrute is a psych rock collective out of Atlanta featuring Alo Ver’s ethereal vocals\, which complement the band’s deep pocket grooves and iridescent soundscapes.\n\n\nOrbiting around Asheville’s grateful music scene since late 2023\, Suns Of Stars blends contemporary and traditional bluegrass with a high energy jam style.\nAt its core lies the trio of Alex Bazemore (guitar)\, and Asheville’s own Jackson Chisholm (upright bass) and Johnny Humphries (mandolin)\, son of local Bluegrass legend Don Humphries. As Suns Of Stars has been gathering momentum they’ve picked up Alex Ball (fiddle) and Jason Flournoy (banjo). Suns Of Stars members are all hometown heros in various musical projects around town which has led to great turnout at their shows. That\, along with a massive song repertoire and growing list of original music make for a unique performance each time.\n\n\nFireside Collective has become a true hybrid\, with a strong foundation in bluegrass and folk\, and healthy doses of rock n’ roll and funk\, all blended together in a unique and colorful amalgam of original music.\n\nStrictly Liquid is a musical collaboration of creative spirits blending funky\, psychedelic jams and rock and roll through improv!
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/coming-july-18th-19th-all-jammed-up-music-festival/2026-07-12/
LOCATION:One World Brewing – West\, 520 Haywood Rd\, Asheville\, North Carolina\, 28806
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/726432063_122181129674863612_4849040984687660133_n-e1783090880691.jpg
GEO:35.5783642;-82.5848526
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=One World Brewing – West 520 Haywood Rd Asheville North Carolina 28806;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=520 Haywood Rd:geo:-82.5848526,35.5783642
END:VEVENT
